{
 "schema": "aylmer-poses",
 "version": 1,
 "notes": [
  "x is east, z is SOUTH (tools/build_map.py projection). yaw is the game camera yaw in radians: an eye pose looking at compass heading h has yaw = -h; a chase pose is the CAR yaw, forward = (sin yaw, cos yaw), so heading h means yaw = PI - h.",
  "Eye poses: free camera at the ground height under (x, z) plus `eye` metres, car not drawn, HUD, pedestrians and avatars hidden. fov is the vertical field of view in radians for a 1280x800 frame whose centred crop (`crop`, the reference aspect) spans `hfov`. `ref` is the 2009 reference, relative to CMP_REF_ROOT.",
  "Chase poses: the car is placed at (x, z) facing yaw on the road and the game camera (`camera`: chase or hood) settles behind it. The car is drawn. No crop: the full 1280x800 frame is what the player sees.",
  "regions: tagged rectangles [x0,y0,x1,y1] as fractions of the shot (the cropped frame for eye poses), the lawn, road, wall and sky samples tools/qa/look-diff.mjs compares with assets/look/palette.json. They are outlined on the AFTER panel of every contact sheet, so a wrong one is visible; move them here."
 ],
